#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:1
msgid "Release 2.27.0 (2025-03-03)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:3
msgid ""
"`inputs.self.submodules` flake attribute [\\#12421](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/12421)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:5
msgid ""
"Flakes in Git repositories can now declare that they need Git submodules to "
"be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:11
msgid ""
"Thus, it's no longer needed for the caller of the flake to pass `submodules "
"= true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:13
msgid ""
"Git LFS support [\\#10153](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10153) "
"[\\#12468](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12468)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:15
msgid ""
"The Git fetcher now supports Large File Storage (LFS). This can be enabled "
"by passing the attribute `lfs = true` to the fetcher, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:16
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix flake prefetch 'git+ssh://git@github.com/Apress/repo-with-large-file-"
"storage.git?lfs=1'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:20
msgid "A flake can also declare that it requires LFS to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:27
msgid ""
"Author: [**@b-camacho**](https://github.com/b-camacho), [**@kip93**](https://"
"github.com/kip93)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:29
msgid ""
"Handle the case where a chroot store is used and some inputs are in the "
"\"host\" `/nix/store` [\\#12512](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12512)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:31
msgid ""
"The evaluator now presents a \"union\" filesystem view of the `/nix/store` "
"in the host and the chroot."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:33
msgid ""
"This change also removes some hacks that broke `builtins.{path,filterSource}"
"` in chroot stores [\\#11503](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/11503)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:35
msgid ""
"`nix flake prefetch` now has a `--out-link` option [\\#12443](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/12443)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:37
msgid ""
"Set `FD_CLOEXEC` on sockets created by curl [\\#12439](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12439)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:39
msgid ""
"Curl created sockets without setting `FD_CLOEXEC`/`SOCK_CLOEXEC`. This could "
"previously cause connections to remain open forever when using commands like "
"`nix shell`. This change sets the `FD_CLOEXEC` flag using a "
"`CURLOPT_SOCKOPTFUNCTION` callback."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:41
msgid ""
"Add BLAKE3 hash algorithm [\\#12379](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12379)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.27.md:43
msgid ""
"Nix now supports the BLAKE3 hash algorithm as an experimental feature "
"(`blake3-hashes`):"
msgstr ""

